# Experiment A′ claims (EQBuddy lab, trap 70). Tracking this file would turn
# every kick into a git conflict, the mailbox rebase war in JSON form.
.claude/soft-seats/claims.json
.claude/soft-seats/*.lock
.claude/soft-seats/*.tmp

# DRA-153: the midnight ExO kick (exo_maturity_midnight_kick.py, Hermes dranak
# profile) writes both of these into the seat WORKTREE ROOT, not a temp dir:
#   .kick-logs/  the seat's own stdout/stderr + last-kick.json (DRA-94 death
#                artifacts, ~1 MB a night)
#   PROMPT.txt   the night's generated seat prompt
# Neither is tracked anywhere, so without these rules a seat's `git add -A`
# commits session transcripts to its branch. PROMPT.txt is root-anchored
# because the name is generic; .kick-logs is not, because the name is not.
.kick-logs/
/PROMPT.txt
